WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:03.190
Use the internet and apps wisely and safely.

2
00:00:03.540 --> 00:00:10.210
This is the video for Module 3 of Smartphone and Digital Awareness: using the internet and helpful apps.

3
00:00:11.460 --> 00:00:19.660
Your phone can do far more than chat. With a browser such as Chrome, you can read news, fill forms and follow an online course.

4
00:00:20.910 --> 00:00:26.350
A few safety habits protect your photos, chats and money, even when you make a mistake.

5
00:00:27.600 --> 00:00:30.840
Free tools like the calculator need no data at all.

6
00:00:32.090 --> 00:00:37.270
And a little checking before you install an app or post online saves a lot of trouble.

7
00:00:38.520 --> 00:00:46.540
The address bar does two jobs. Type an exact address like who dot int to go straight there, or type search words to get results.

8
00:00:47.790 --> 00:00:56.350
Results marked Sponsored are adverts. For official information, prefer government sites, often ending in dot gov dot n g.

9
00:00:57.600 --> 00:01:08.120
Save important pages with the star in the menu. Opening your bank from your own bookmark is safer, because fake look-alike sites sometimes appear in search adverts.

10
00:01:09.370 --> 00:01:21.530
When you download a form, find it later in the Files app, in the Downloads folder. For example, Zainab in Kaduna downloads a scholarship form, then renames it so she can find it by search.

11
00:01:22.780 --> 00:01:27.020
One. A real screen lock, such as a PIN of at least six digits.

12
00:01:28.270 --> 00:01:32.560
Two. Install updates. They fix security holes that criminals use.

13
00:01:33.810 --> 00:01:44.860
Three. Google Play Protect checks your apps. Most dangerous apps arrive as APK files through WhatsApp links. If your phone asks to install unknown apps, say no.

14
00:01:46.110 --> 00:01:52.170
Four. Check permissions. Does this app need my contacts, location or SMS to do its job?

15
00:01:53.420 --> 00:01:58.410
Five. Switch on Google backup, Google Photos backup and WhatsApp chat backup.

16
00:01:59.660 --> 00:02:05.020
Six. Switch on Find My Device, so you can ring, lock or erase a lost phone.

17
00:02:06.270 --> 00:02:21.580
For example, Funmi in Ilorin opens Permission manager. A free torchlight app has access to her contacts, location and SMS. A torch needs none of that, and her phone already has a flashlight tile, so she uninstalls it.

18
00:02:22.830 --> 00:02:33.410
WhatsApp needs the microphone for voice notes, but only while she uses it. So she changes it to Allow only while using the app. The whole check took about ten minutes.

19
00:02:34.660 --> 00:02:42.470
The Calculator app is already on your phone and needs no data. For example, Esther in Makurdi checks the trader's bill.

20
00:02:43.720 --> 00:02:53.730
Noodles at about 7,500 naira, oil at about 3,200 naira, and seasoning at about 1,800 naira.

21
00:02:54.980 --> 00:03:14.070
The total is 12,500 naira. The trader offers 10% off, so she uses the percent button and gets 1,250 naira. She pays 11,250 naira, and counts 3,750 naira change from 15,000 naira.

22
00:03:14.420 --> 00:03:18.920
The history button shows every step she typed, so she knows the numbers are right.

23
00:03:20.170 --> 00:03:30.140
Before you install, check the developer is the real company, for example the bank's own name for a bank app. Be wary of a famous name with very few downloads.

24
00:03:30.490 --> 00:03:37.550
Read recent low-star reviews, check the Data safety section, and see if there are ads or payments inside.

25
00:03:37.900 --> 00:03:41.800
And remember, uninstalling an app does not cancel its subscription.

26
00:03:43.050 --> 00:03:51.780
You do not need every platform. Choose one or two that fit what you want. Keep your personal account private, and hide your phone number and address.

27
00:03:53.030 --> 00:04:00.260
If an account is fake, a scam, or harassing you, take screenshots, then use the three dots to report and block.

28
00:04:01.510 --> 00:04:12.960
For example, Blessing in Warri spends about 3 hours a day scrolling. She sets app timers for 1 hour a day in total, and wins back about 60 hours a month for her sewing orders.

29
00:04:14.210 --> 00:04:20.490
To remember. Bookmark your bank. Keep the six safety habits. Check an app page before you install it.

30
00:04:20.840 --> 00:04:26.570
Keep personal accounts private, and before you post, ask: is it true, and is it mine to share?

31
00:04:27.820 --> 00:04:37.490
In this module you will practise browsing, do your six-habit safety check, put four free tools to work, tidy your apps, and set up social media safely.

32
00:04:37.840 --> 00:04:39.780
Continue with the lessons below.
